#
# FR-020 / AC-025 — the bulk-GRIND hole. Every bulk_grind_* name builds a REAL
# throwaway git repository whose HEAD moved past a stamped .cast-baseline-sha,
# because the context comes from `git diff --name-only baseline..HEAD` and a
# mocked diff would only prove the mock agrees with the test author:
#   ..._bulk_grind_returns_grind_cycle_context_per_casting     the fix
#   ..._bulk_cast_returns_no_grind_cycle_context               still GRIND-only
#   ..._bulk_grind_matches_the_single_spawn_path_it_was_missing  one builder, both paths
#
# GRIND cycle 4 closed the same loop for the two cases the write half was
# missing. D-022 — the DONE status is unreachable from the read side unless
# the emitted prompt asks the agent for a terminal line:
#   ..._a_terminal_line_written_as_instructed_reports_done   round trip, both
#                                                            halves, no literals
